From edc33195c461ef11c70a4a657813f998dcaa067f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@localhost.localdomain>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:18:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] syscall: answer stat, fstat, and statx at seccomp enter stop

Under seccomp acceleration (seccomp_after_ptrace_enter), newfstatat,
fstatat64, fstat, and statx are filtered with FILTER_SYSEXIT so
fake_id0 and link2symlink can adjust their results at sysexit.  Even
after recent exit-stage optimizations, every call still pays a second
ptrace stop and context switch.

Answer safe native ABI_DEFAULT calls directly during the seccomp enter
stop via a new STAT_SYSCALL extension event (and the existing
STATX_SYSCALL event), voiding the syscall with PR_void and skipping the
sysexit stop with PTRACE_CONT:

- tracee/event.c & tracee.h: allow FILTER_SYSEXIT syscalls to skip
  the sysexit stop when seccomp_after_ptrace_enter is active,
  sysexit_necessary is false, and the enter stage answered the call.
- extension.h, fake_id0, link2symlink: introduce STAT_SYSCALL with a
  struct stat_syscall_state { host_path, stat_buf } so core code stays
  decoupled from extensions.  fake_id0 updates st_uid/st_gid (and
  falls back with -ENOSYS under USERLAND); link2symlink updates
  st_nlink for backing files and falls back with -EAGAIN for unresolved
  link2symlink symlinks.
- tracee/statx.c & syscall/enter.c: handle newfstatat/fstatat64, fstat
  (via pidfd_open + pidfd_getfd), and statx (reusing the already
  translated host path in CURRENT SYSARG_2, or pidfd_getfd for
  AT_EMPTY_PATH).  Unusual flags, /proc paths, non-native ABIs,
  chained syscalls, 32-bit ARM (where the kernel runs SYSCALL_AVOIDER),
  and host errors other than ENOENT/ENOTDIR fall back to the normal
  enter+exit path.

Tested on ARM64 Android (Termux + Ubuntu 24.04 PRoot): all stat,
smoke, and link2symlink/fake_id0 checks match upstream with 0 diff;
microbenchmarks improve by 36-45% and fstat context switches drop
by 50%.

Assisted-By: LLM
